# Patches are applied with git apply, which requires the exact bytes the patch was
# generated with. A CRLF checkout breaks every hunk with "patch does not apply",
# which is what happened to patches/xnu/vermeer-4k-block-split-hint.patch before
# this file existed. UniXNU's own .gitattributes carries the same rule.
*.patch text eol=lf -whitespace
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# Firmware and device tree inputs are binary; never touch their bytes.
*.dtb binary
*.bin binary
*.img binary
